.TH "DOTFILES-CI" "7" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
dotfiles-ci \- GitHub Actions pipelines, release publication and credential checklist
.SH DESCRIPTION
The repository defines its main build, verification and release workflow
in .github/workflows/ci.yml. It runs on main/master pushes,
pull requests, selected version tags, schedules and manual dispatch.
The workflow routes each event to the required checks, image build,
release packaging, and tag publication tasks. It is not a general
purpose signing or secret provisioning system.
.SH WORKFLOW MODES
.TP
\fBlint-fix\fR
Default manual dispatch mode. Runs the nightly maintenance path and
checks.
.TP
\fBbuild\fR
Run code checks and the container build without publishing.
.TP
\fBrelease-patch, release-minor, release-major\fR
Prepare the requested stable version tag from main, then dispatch
the release workflow on that tag.
.TP
\fBrelease-test, release-rc, release-alpha\fR
Prepare a prerelease/test version tag for the corresponding release
path. Prereleases do not advance the stable latest image alias.
.TP
\fBpublish-tag\fR
Recover or publish an existing release tag. Dispatch against that
tag, not main. The workflow requires a v* or test-* ref.
.TP
\fBmonthly-maintenance\fR
Run the monthly maintenance path. Scheduled runs also invoke
monthly and nightly branches independently.
.PP
Optional dispatch inputs include release_version_override,
force_release and allow_prs. force_release requests a fresh pull
and uncached image build; it cannot override pinned Dockerfile
dependencies.
.SH CREDENTIALS, KEYS AND PERMISSIONS
The current ci.yml uses the ephemeral GitHub Actions-provided
\fBGITHUB_TOKEN\fR for the secret scanner, GitHub Release publishing
and GHCR docker/login-action. Its manual tag-dispatch step uses
\fBGH_TOKEN\fR populated from github.token. These are generated for
the workflow run and are not secret values kept in Git history.
.PP
The workflow declares permissions including contents:write,
pull-requests:write, checks:write, packages:write and
security-events:write. Some jobs override those permissions,
for example the Docker publish job needs packages:write and
the tag-preparation job needs contents:write plus actions:write.
Repository Actions settings, fork event restrictions, branch/tag
rules and package visibility can still prevent writes.
.PP
No additional manually defined secrets are directly referenced in
the currently inspected ci.yml. Do not assume that all current or
future workflows are credential-free: inspect ALL workflows and
GitHub Actions Environments, repository/organization Secrets and
Variables, branch/tag restrictions, package credentials and any
deploy or signing keys before restoring, forking or migrating a
pipeline. Git cloning and copying YAML do not copy GitHub-hosted
secret values or deployment keys.
.PP
When a pipeline acquires an external credential, document its
\fBname, purpose, scope, source, provisioning location, expiration
or rotation procedure and failure symptoms\fR. Never commit the
credential value, paste it into README/man pages, print it in CI
logs or distribute it in rendered dotfiles or archives. Keep
credentials scoped to the consuming environment.
.SH HOW RELEASE PUBLISHING WORKS
Code checks (including ShellCheck, chezmoi smoke application and
gitleaks) gate the release. A tag build publishes the development
container to GHCR and packages the chezmoi rendered release ZIP.
The publish-release job creates GitHub Release assets from
successful release artifacts. The release ZIP may contain runner
specific generated settings: use chezmoi init for real machine
bootstrap instead of treating it as a portable configured home.
.PP
A successful PR merge or main-branch CI run alone does not publish
a new container release. The latest image tag advances only with
a qualifying stable release. An old retained development container
cannot update its creation-time mounts or image merely by restarting.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gh auth status
gh workflow list --repo arran4/dotfiles
gh workflow run ci.yml --repo arran4/dotfiles --ref main \
  -f mode=build
gh workflow run ci.yml --repo arran4/dotfiles --ref main \
  -f mode=release-patch
gh workflow run ci.yml --repo arran4/dotfiles --ref main \
  -f mode=release-patch -f force_release=true
gh workflow run ci.yml --repo arran4/dotfiles --ref v1.2.3 \
  -f mode=publish-tag
gh run list --repo arran4/dotfiles --workflow ci.yml
.fi
.PP
The v1.2.3 tag above is a placeholder: replace it with an existing
release tag that actually belongs to this repository.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
For failed publication, inspect the tag/ref and job logs, then
check repository workflow token permissions and GHCR package access.
A release-* dispatch prepares and pushes a tag; a separate
publish-tag dispatch performs publication. A failure between them
may require explicit publish-tag recovery.
.PP
For cloning or migration, record which credentials and permissions
must be recreated outside the repository before assuming the CI is
operational. Do not diagnose failed authentication by printing secret
values. Local gh auth and GitHub Actions GITHUB_TOKEN are distinct
credential contexts.
